# Tech Stack

- Use TypeScript
- Use Node.js
- Use Telegraf
- Use async/await only
- Use ESM modules

# Architecture

- Keep handlers separated
- Keep API logic in services/
- Keep bot initialization in bot.ts
- Avoid large files

# Code Style

- Prefer small pure functions
- Use explicit types
- Avoid any
- Prefer const over let
- Use early returns
- Use try/catch for async flows

# Telegram Rules

- Use reply keyboard for main actions
- Always answer user actions
- Show loading message before image generation
- Handle Telegram API errors

# Pollinations API Rules

- Keep API logic isolated in services/pollinations.ts
- Encode prompts properly
- Handle network failures
- Use configurable timeout

# Error Handling

- Never crash the bot
- Log all unexpected errors
- Return friendly user messages

# Forbidden

- No database
- No classes unless necessary
- No global mutable state
- No huge handler files
- No business logic inside bot.ts
